Modifications by the Treyrin project include the cognitive core, decoder
connections, LoRA/output adaptation, experience and hypothesis state,
goal/action computation, checkpoint assembly and native-format conversion.
Language weights are modified/adapted; Q8_0 also quantizes the language tensors.
The upstream vision encoder is excluded.

The runtime includes modified llama.cpp/ggml code under its MIT license and
separately licensed dependencies. Upstream notices and dependency licenses
are preserved in runtime/source and in the binary runtime archive.
